Cell["\<\
The residual q2=p3-ell fixes Delta ell-minus~delta^3 and Delta \
ell-perp~delta^2. Consequently ell has local widths (6,3,2). Since 6+3>2*2, \
this is a genuine transverse-dominated Glauber integration mode. There is one \
Glauber loop, not two. Its central powers (2,2,0) and its fluctuation widths \
(6,3,2) are deliberately shown in separate columns. For the other loop, q0 \
and q1=p1-r analogously pinch r-plus between opposite half-planes and confirm \
Delta r-plus~delta^6.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f625322c-0103-4a6b-9091-54f8047434eb"],

